Let 
$F_n \ (n \in \mathbb N),\,F_\infty$ be closed subsets in $\mathbb C$.  
We say that the sequence $F_n$ converges $F_\infty$ in the sense of Hausdorff 
if the following two conditions are satisfied: 
\begin{enumerate}
\item For any $x_\infty \in F_\infty$, there is a sequence $x_n \in F_n$ 
such that $x_n \to x_\infty$. 
\item If there is a sequence 
$x_{n_j} \in F_{n_j}$ such that $x_{n_j} \to x_\infty$, then  $x_\infty \in F_\infty$. 
\end{enumerate}

